```
That same function also rejects spec URNs symmetrically at [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store.rs#L229-L255).

2. `DefaultTicketStateResolver` is defined at [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store.rs#L187-L190). The full resolver body is [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store.rs#L193-L255). It does not open a store itself; it uses `self.store`, which is created earlier by `default_ticket_state_resolver()` via `TicketStore::open_or_init(&self.ticket_store_root())` in [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store/config/persistence.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store/config/persistence.rs#L203-L215). The store root comes from `ticket_store_root()`, which returns `sibling_store_root(&self.root, ".ticket")` at [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store/config/persistence.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store/config/persistence.rs#L184-L186).

3. The session workspace slug is `SessionStoreConfig.workspace_slug` in [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store.rs#L102-L106). It is passed into `SessionStoreConfig::new(store_root.clone(), args.workspace_slug)` in [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/bin/copilot-capture-hook.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/bin/copilot-capture-hook.rs#L65-L71), and the CLI default is `"default"` in [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/bin/copilot-capture-hook/args.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/bin/copilot-capture-hook/args.rs#L21-L25) and [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/bin/copilot-capture-hook/args.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/bin/copilot-capture-hook/args.rs#L65-L69). The resolver copies that field into `DefaultTicketStateResolver.workspace_slug` at [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store/config/persistence.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store/config/persistence.rs#L203-L215).

4. The URN parser is `parse_entity_urn()` returning `ParsedEntityUrn` in [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store_routing_types.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/store_routing_types.rs#L32-L70). It parses `ce://<workspace>/<store>/<entity>` into `workspace_slug`, `kind`, and `entity_id`, mapping `ticket|tickets` to ticket, `spec|specs` to spec, and `rule|rules` to rule.

5. There is no existing slug-to-ticket-store-root registry in the ticket MCP path or session-api config. `ticket-mcp` resolves `workspace` as either `"default"` or a filesystem path: [memory-api/tools/mcp/ticket-mcp/src/server.rs](memory-api/tools/mcp/ticket-mcp/src/server.rs#L99-L132) calls `resolve_store_root_from(Path::new(workspace), TICKET_INDEX_DIR)` and never looks up a slug registry. Its workspace list is only `["default", active_path]` at [memory-api/tools/mcp/ticket-mcp/src/server/query.rs](memory-api/tools/mcp/ticket-mcp/src/server/query.rs#L22-L31). I found no `WorkspaceRegistry`-style slug mapper in `memory-api/crates/**` or `memory-api/tools/mcp/ticket-mcp/src/**`; the only `WorkspaceRegistry` hit is in `memory-api/crates/memory-matrix/src/http.rs`, where it wraps a single opened store, not a slug lookup.

